 {
  "id": "C19",
  "title": "The failure signature uses the first line containing 'fail' or 'error', often an echoed action input",
  "file": "src/integrations/ci-classifier.ts",
  "A": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "A job log that echoes an action input such as 'fail-on-cache-miss: false' before the real failure gets that echo line as its recorded 'failing line'. The ledger then records the same meaningless line for every failure of that check.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun test $TMPDIR/adj052/repro.test.ts (test 'C19': ciSignature over a log with an actions/cache input echo, then 'FAIL src/a.test.ts')",
    "output": "C19 fail-on-cache-miss: false"
   },
   "evidence": "ci-classifier.ts:44: `lines.find((l) => /timed out after|##\\[error\\]|\\b(?:error|fail(?:ed|ure)?)\\b/i.test(l))` picks the first match, and `\\bfail\\b` matches 'fail-on-cache-miss'."
  },
  "B": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "An action prints a normal input containing the word fail before tests run. Different test failures then receive the same ledger identity, obscuring their causes and conflating their retry allowances.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun \"$TMPDIR/ci-adjudication.ts\"",
    "output": "C19: test A and test B both selected line=\"fail-on-cache-miss: false\" and signature=[\"test\",\"fail-on-cache-miss: false\",\"ubuntu-24.04\"]; collide=true"
   },
   "evidence": "HEAD selects the first line matching '/timed out after|##\\[error\\]|\\b(?:error|fail(?:ed|ure)?)\\b/i'. A hyphen is a word boundary, so fail-on-cache-miss matches before the actual error. This does not exceed the numerical cap; it incorrectly merges distinct failures under that cap. The signature function is new."
  }
 },
